src/DEPG0213BN.py

MicroPython driver for the DEPG0213BN e-paper panel fitted to the LILYGO TTGO
T5. The executable code is identical to upstream; this copy omits some blocks
of commented-out C++ that upstream keeps for reference. Upstream is MIT
licensed and the copy here has no licence header of its own, so the terms come
from the upstream repository.

    Copyright (c) 2021 Inqbus
    https://github.com/Inqbus/micropython_DEPG0213BN

One part of the file deserves a separate note. The 153-byte partial-refresh
waveform table, PART_UPDATE_LUT_TTGO_DKE, and the command sequence around it
are the ones found in lewisxhe's fork of GxEPD (GxDEPG0213BN.cpp) and in
ESPHome's waveshare_epaper component, both of which are GPL-3.0 C++ projects;
the upstream author translated them to Python and published the result as MIT.
The table is controller configuration data for the panel rather than program
logic. It is carried here on that understanding, and this note exists so that
nobody has to rediscover where it came from.

    https://github.com/lewisxhe/GxEPD
    https://github.com/esphome/esphome

